From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:47:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] sf_smac: run the channel switch works under the wiphy mutex

Two works around channel switches can run into freed memory.

The CSA completion (siwifi_csa_finish(), and siwifi_acs_csa_finish() for
the internal ACS) is queued from the firmware's CSA-finish indication
and frees the struct siwifi_csa that contains it. siwifi_del_csa()
frees the same struct from stop_ap, from a new channel switch and from
the firmware restart path, without cancelling the work. A stop_ap while
the completion is queued or running leaves it working on freed memory.
A plain cancel_work_sync() in siwifi_del_csa() is not possible: the
completion takes the wiphy mutex, which stop_ap already holds.

The internal ACS queues siwifi_hw->csa_work, which walks the interfaces
and starts channel switches without any lock. Nothing cancels it when
the driver is unloaded.

Make both wiphy works. They then run under the wiphy mutex, so they
cannot run while a cfg80211 operation is in progress. siwifi_del_csa()
can drop a queued completion with wiphy_work_cancel(), and
wiphy_unregister() deals with a pending ACS work. Initialise the
completion when the CSA is allocated, because the error paths of the
channel switch free it before the old INIT_WORK() was reached. Take the
wiphy mutex in the restart path around the part that frees the CSA.

Signed-off-by: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
---
 sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_acs.c  | 23 +++++++++----------
 sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_acs.h  |  2 +-
